% 28 Sep 2026). Real-time reflection-aware RGB-D Gaussian SLAM for indoor
% scenes. First real-time GS-SLAM to explicitly model planar reflections:
% a reflection-aware TSDF-Gaussian hybrid representation separates diffuse
% base appearance (TSDF volume + base Gaussians) from reflection components
% (reflection groups = reflective plane + virtual-space reflection Gaussians).
% Three-pass rendering: TSDF raycast (color/depth/plane-ID/reflection-mask) →
% order-independent base-Gaussian render with depth culling → plane-ID-guided
% reflection-Gaussian rasterization, composited via reflection mask.
% Reflection-aware tracking excludes reflection-dominated regions (initial
% point-to-plane ICP pose, then reflection-intensity masking). Reflective
% planes detected by combining geometry (CAPE plane segmentation), semantics
% (Grounded SAM2), and a temporal raycast color-variance cue, aggregated in a
% sliding window. Outperforms GPS-SLAM / GS-ICP SLAM / RTG-SLAM in
% reconstruction quality, tracking robustness, and novel-view rendering under
% strong planar reflections while staying real-time. Peripheral to
% Gaussian-LIC2 (RGB-D indoor, no LiDAR/inertial), but relevant to the
% appearance-modeling thread — the reflection/base separation is a transferable
% idea for LIV GS-SLAM scenes with specular surfaces (glass facades, wet
