% MAGS-SLAM (Cao, Shao, Zhai, Zhang, Nguyen, Wang, Huang; ETH Zurich +
% Liverpool + Harbin Eng + Ottawa + Wuhan + SJTU + Imperial; arXiv:2605.10760,
% v1 11 May 2026, v2 27 Jul 2026). The first monocular RGB-only multi-agent
% 3DGS SLAM framework. Each agent independently runs a DROID-BA monocular
% front-end with Joint Depth-Scale Adjustment (JDSA) coupling Metric3D-v2
% monocular depth priors into dense bundle adjustment, incrementally builds
% local Gaussian submaps, and exchanges compact submap summaries (128-D
% DROID descriptor + <=512 sparse 3D points + downsampled registration cloud
% + AABB + anchor keyframe) instead of raw observations. A communication-
% efficient coordinator establishes cross-agent constraints via cosine
% retrieval, hybrid sparse+LoFTR matching, RANSAC Umeyama Sim(3), spatial-
% extent gate, and ICP refinement, then solves a global Sim(3) submap pose
% graph (MaPGBA) coupling geometric and anchor-image photometric residuals.
% Asynchronous occupancy-aware fusion deduplicates borrowed Gaussians against
% target-agent occupied + free-space voxels (0.10 m voxel, 64-bit spatial
% hash), followed by joint pose-Gaussian photometric refinement with per-
% keyframe exposure compensation. On ReplicaMultiagent, RGB-only achieves
% 43.24 dB PSNR — exceeding all RGB-D collaborative baselines (CoMA-SLAM,
% MAC-Ego3D, MAGiC-SLAM, GRAND-SLAM); on AriaMultiagent (3 agents) mean ATE
% 0.54 cm beats MAGiC-SLAM RGB-D 0.65 cm; on ETH3D +5 dB PSNR over MAC-Ego3D.
% Ablation: removing Sim(3) scale (degenerate to SE(3)) drops PSNR 21.72 dB
% — scale alignment is the single most critical component; occupancy-aware
% fusion second (-7.17 dB). Releases ReplicaMultiagent Plus benchmark (4
% agents, long-horizon trajectories, GT geometry + semantic annotations).
