% SA-LIVO (Cao, He, Zhu, ..., Wang; arXiv:2606.25699 v2 6 Aug 2026, v1 24
% Jun 2026). Subspace-Aware LIVO: addresses the independent-failure-mode
% problem in tightly-coupled LIVO (LiDAR degeneracy when scan geometry is
% under-constrained; vision degradation under poor illumination / texture
% absence) which existing modality-level countermeasures (binary
% degeneracy detection, covariance inflation, scene-level quality gating)
% cannot resolve directionally. SAIF (Subspace-Aware Information Fusion)
% eigendecomposes the joint LiDAR-visual information matrix and gates each
% eigendirection by a single-threshold linear clamp, attenuating
% degenerate directions while passing well-observed ones at full
% strength; robust per-residual gating + a scene-level quality factor
% screen corrupted measurements. LiDAR and visual residuals share one
% InEKF loop at a shared linearization point (eliminating sequential-
% update mismatch), and photometric Jacobians are assembled once before
% the loop and reused across iterations (visual information contributes
% only where LiDAR is deficient). On 29 sequences (HILTI'22, Newer
% College, Oxford Spires) + concurrent-degradation scenarios: competitive
% accuracy, bounded drift where R3LIVE / SR-LIVO diverge; 12.3 ms/frame
% laptop CPU, 26.8 ms embedded ARM without GPU, 3.6-6.3x lower peak
% memory. Directly relevant to Gaussian-LIC2: same FAST-LIVO2 LIVO
% lineage; the direction-selective subspace-aware fusion is the
# principled degeneracy-handling counterpart to ad-hoc modality gating,
% transferable to a LIV GS-SLAM where LiDAR and visual residuals must be
% fused per-direction under geometric / photometric degradation, and the
% single-loop InEKF with reused photometric Jacobians is an efficiency
% pattern relevant to embedded cooperative-node deployment. Cite in the
